{"shortDescription":"Asia fuel oil markets softened on Tuesday, with spot premiums sliding day on day while prompt timespreads logged a narrower backwardation for both very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) and high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO).A physical trade for Singapore VLSFO emerged at a weaker premium versus the previous…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia fuel oil markets softened on Tuesday, with spot premiums sliding day on day while prompt timespreads logged a narrower backwardation for both very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) and high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO)."]},{"type":"p","children":["A physical trade for Singapore VLSFO emerged at a weaker premium versus the previous session for December loading dates."]},{"type":"p","children":["Outside the window, Nigeria's Dangote had offered low-sulphur straight-run fuel for loading in early December, according to industry sources. The tender closes on Tuesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, trading momentum for HSFO was broadly thin, though timespreads continued to sell off for prompt December/January contracts."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cracks traded lower, with the 380-cst HSFO December crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) easing to a discount wider than $6 a barrel on Tuesday, while the VLSFO crack (LFO05SGBRTCMc1) slipped below a premium of $19 a barrel, showed LSEG data."]},{"type":"p","children":["The hi-5 fuel oil spread (FO05-380SGMc1) narrowed from the previous close, ending the Tuesday session near $159 a metric ton for the December contract."]},{"type":"p","children":["REFINERY UPDATES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Nigeria's Securities and Exchange Commission approved Dangote Refinery's plan for allocating shares in its heavily oversubscribed initial public offering that closed last month, three people familiar with the matter said."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices extended their falls into a second day on Tuesday on signs of rising 